e already asked for B's missing info and got none. So we cannot fill.\n\nThus we might keep B as leading candidate, but note that we need to consider C's strong decision quality and reliability.\n\nWe can argue that despite B's communication concerns, they can be mitigated, while C's egocentric and lack of adaptability may be more problematic.\n\nThus we maintain recommendation for B, but suggest we need to discuss C further.\n\nSo our public message: I agree with B, but highlight missing evidence for B and bring up C's strengths and concerns, and suggest we still need to discuss C and D.\n\nWe need to reference the fact that we have no info on B's decision speed etc, and that C is 100% reliable, quick decisions, excellent attention, positive crew atmosphere.\n\nThus we can argue that B remains best, but we need to consider C.\n\nWe must include our vote in metadata: Candidate B.\n\nProceed."}
